            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial ischemia due to a coronary-pulmonary fistula treated with coil embolization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>551-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe one case of myocardial ischemia due to a coronary-pulmonary fistula, successfully treated with coils. Coronary fistulae are a rare cause of angina in adults with normal coronary arteries. Percutaneous treatment represents an alternative to surgery and may be offered as a relatively low risk procedure. The choice between surgical and percutaneous treatment must take into account clinical and anatomical considerations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
